.SH NAME
.PP
thruk - monitoring webinterface for nagios, icinga and shinken
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Thruk is a monitoring web interface for multiple backends.
It supports Nagios, Icinga and Shinken through the Livestatus API.
It is designed as a `dropin' replacement and covers almost all original
features.
It also adds features for large installations.
.PP
Access Thruk at http://host/thruk/.
.PP
The default account is `thrukadmin'.
The package ships it without a password, so it is disabled until you set
one:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
htpasswd /etc/thruk/htpasswd thrukadmin
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
Package upgrades disable only the shipped legacy default password.
They preserve operator-set passwords and other accounts.
.PP
You probably need to change the backend configuration in
/etc/thruk/thruk_local.conf.
